      "id": "claim_dc09bdaed83e48e99e725a448cf88c8b",
      "statement": "The MCP side opens a fresh WebSocket per tool call via requestBrijio in websocket-client.ts: it authenticates with the pairing token, sends the envelope after auth_success, waits for the matching response or timeout, then closes the socket. The extension side, by contrast, holds one persistent WebSocket owned by BrijioBackgroundController.",
